## Review detection checklist

> **Purpose:** After scoping sections, walk this table for **every** matching file type. Each row names a **Standard** label (from `skills/lmap-code-review/SKILL.md`) and concrete patterns to search for. Do not skip rows because critical issues were already found.

### Mandatory execution (directory-wide and large reviews)

1. For **each** checklist row whose file-type column matches a file under review, run a repository search (`Grep` / `rg`) for the patterns in the third column — do not rely on memory or skimming.
2. **Every pattern match is at least one finding** (or split into separate findings when issues are unrelated). Tag with the row's **Standard** label; do not report SQL injection or `@` suppression without a label.
3. When a row's patterns are searched and absent, note `Standard: <label> — searched, no match` under **Checklist traceability** in the review output.
4. Controllers, **all** `src/Service/**` classes (not only `*Service.php`), repositories, helpers, and listeners all need SQL-injection and abstraction scans.
5. After grep passes, run the **Manual review pass** (below) for labels marked `manual` in **Checklist coverage** — grep alone missed real violations in practice (god classes, `mail()`, hard-coded `PEPPER` constants, unpaginated `fetchAllEntitiesForGrid`, in-place migration edits, GET/POST resolution drift, etc.).
6. Run the **Diff-context passes** (below) on every branch/PR review — these catch issues grep cannot (modified vs new migrations, paired controller actions, Twig component reuse).
7. In **Checklist traceability**, list **every** Standard label from `skills/lmap-code-review/SKILL.md` — either `N finding(s)` or `searched, no match` / `manual pass, no match`.

